  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_019 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) at 0.639 acc. We've established that multiprofile >> singleprofile, avgpool > transformer, and weighted > concat fusion. The image encoder choice (resnet50 vs imagenet_vit_l) appears nearly irrelevant (0.639 vs 0.635). However, the RNA encoder has only ever been pca_n2000 across all six experiments—this is the largest unexplored design axis. Question: Does a learned, biologically-informed RNA encoder (scgpt) outperform PCA in the best-performing multimodal configuration? This experiment changes only the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scgpt while holding all other settings at their empirically best values (multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, weighted). Why this is the best next experiment: Under a limited budget, testing the single most impactful unexplored variable in the known-best configuration maximizes information gain. If scgpt improves, it opens a productive direction; if it does not, it confirms PCA sufficiency and redirects exploration toward other axes (e.g., transformer+weighted, or image-only baselines) with greater confidence."
}

